Description: Bande Settings: panes for the desktop and its devices with ranked search
 Settings of the Bande desktop in four groups: Connections (Wi-Fi with
 known networks, per-network details and hidden networks, Bluetooth,
 network), Desktop (appearance and wallpaper, the bar, notifications per
 app, accessibility), Devices (displays, sound, keyboard, trackpad and
 mouse) and System (power, users and groups, apps that open at login,
 language and time, about this computer with storage and software
 update), with a search field that ranks the matching settings and marks
 them. Every pane follows changes made elsewhere while it is open.
 Desktop settings go through org.bande.Config, which writes config.kdl. A
 polkit rule lets administrators (members of sudo) change the time,
 language, login screen keyboard layouts and computer name without a
 password prompt. Any supported language can be chosen; it is generated
 with locale-gen. Updates install through PackageKit while the computer
 runs; only those that need a restart install at the next restart,
 through PackageKit's offline updates. Settings asks to log out or reopen
 apps that still run the old version, and never restarts or logs out by
 itself.

