Package: bande-disks
Architecture: any
Built-Using: ${cargo:Built-Using}
Static-Built-Using: ${cargo:Static-Built-Using}
Section: admin
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
 fonts-inter,
 fonts-manrope,
 fonts-jetbrains-mono,
 udisks2,
 ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: dosfstools,
 e2fsprogs,
 exfatprogs
Suggests: ntfs-3g
Description: disk manager for the Bande desktop
 Disks shows the computer's internal and external disks, their partitions
 and volumes and the disk images that are open, with their capacity,
 format, connection and S.M.A.R.T. health. It mounts, unmounts and ejects
 them, erases and partitions disks, checks and repairs volumes, renames
 volumes, creates and restores disk images and writes an image to a USB
 drive. Every change goes through UDisks2 and asks for authorization. The
 disk the computer started up from and the volumes the system uses are
 shown read-only.

Package: bande-archive
Architecture: any
Built-Using: ${cargo:Built-Using}
Static-Built-Using: ${cargo:Static-Built-Using}
Section: utils
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
 fonts-inter,
 fonts-manrope,
 fonts-jetbrains-mono,
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: archive manager for the Bande desktop
 The archive tool of the Bande desktop: expands zip, tar (gzip, bzip2,
 xz, zstd), single gzip, bzip2, xz and zstd files and 7-Zip archives next
 to themselves, asks for the password of encrypted ones, and makes Files'
 Compress in the format chosen in its settings. It refuses items that
 would land outside the folder, decompression bombs and setuid
 permissions.

